    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.46,
      "end_seconds": 273.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "right let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.92,
      "end_seconds": 276.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.95,
      "end_seconds": 289.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "your pulse and blood pressure are normal and you are tearful when talking about work"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.66,
      "end_seconds": 291.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.04,
      "end_seconds": 307.22,
      "duration_seconds": 11.18,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Putting it all together, it fits best with low mood linked to work stress. Another possibility is an anxiety disorder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.28,
      "end_seconds": 312.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Mm is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.68,
      "end_seconds": 346.52,
      "duration_seconds": 32.84,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now low mood linked to work stress is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'm sending you for a thyroid test because of low mood and fatigue. We should do a blood count for fatigue. For this, sertraline, 50 milligrams, once a day, for six weeks then review. You take it by mouth. That's for low mood. Try a short walk each day and keep a regular bedtime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.04,
      "end_seconds": 357.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.75,
      "text": "Do get help quickly if you have thoughts of harming yourself. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.59,
      "end_seconds": 361.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "that's clear, you know, thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.26,
      "end_seconds": 363.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
